Look at the terminal — do you see npm run dev running? 🧱You said: yes i can see home and login but when we click it its refresingyes i can see home and login but when we click it its refresingJun 4Claude responded: Good catch.Good catch. Real engineering thinking. 💪

Why it's refreshing?
You used <a href> — that's normal HTML. It refreshes the page.
In React we use <Link> from react-router-dom. It navigates without refresh.

You fix it yourself:

Import Link from react-router-dom
Replace <a href="/"> with <Link to="/">
Replace <a href="/login"> with <Link to="/login">

Try it. Paste here. 🧱function Navbar() {
  return (
    <nav className="bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-4 flex justify-between items-center">
      <span className="text-xl font-bold">CollabSpace</span>
      <div className="flex gap-4">
        <Link ="/" className="hover:underline">
          Home
        </Link >
        <Link ="/login" className="hover:underline">
          Login
        </Link >
      </div>
    </nav>
  );
}

export default Navbar;Show moreJun 4Claude responded: Two mistakes:Two mistakes:

Mistake 1: Missing import at top:
jsximport { Link } from 'react-router-dom'
Mistake 2: Link needs to keyword:
jsx<Link to="/">
You wrote <Link ="/"> — missing to.

Fix both. Paste here. 🧱You said: done now its working without refresingdone now its working without refresingJun 4Claude responded: 🎉 Perfect.🎉 Perfect.
That's the difference between <a href> and <Link to>. You'll never forget it now.

