Next — Step 4: API Endpoints
Before I explain — you tell me:
What is an API endpoint in simple words? 🧱You said: i don't knowi don't knowJun 6Claude responded: Simple answer:Simple answer:

An endpoint is a URL that does something when you call it.

Examples:
POST /auth/register    → create new user
POST /auth/login       → login user
GET  /workspaces       → get all workspaces
POST /workspaces       → create workspace
HTTP methods:

GET → fetch data
POST → create data
PUT → update data
DELETE → delete data


