Post
Put
deleteJun 6Claude responded: Good.Good. Now add the URLs too.
Like this pattern:
GET  /tasks/...
POST /tasks/...
What comes after /tasks/?
Hint: to update or delete ONE specific task → you need its id in the URL. 🧱You said: GET  /tasks/idGET  /tasks/id
POST /tasks/id
PUT /tasks/id
DELETE/tasks/idJun 6Claude responded: Almost.Almost. Few fixes:
GET    /tasks          → get ALL tasks (no id needed)
GET    /tasks/{id}     → get ONE task
POST   /tasks          → create task (no id, it's new)
PUT    /tasks/{id}     → update ONE task
DELETE /tasks/{id}     → delete ONE task
Rule:

No {id} → working with all items
With {id} → working with one specific item


