SQLAlchemy needs to know about all models before it can create tables in PostgreSQL. If we don't import them → tables never get created.


Now update main.py yourself:
1. import Base from database
2. import engine from database
3. import all models (User, Workspace, Task, Document, InviteCode, WorkspaceMember)
4. call Base.metadata.create_all(bind=engine)
Base.metadata.create_all → this creates all tables in PostgreSQL automatically.
