Model → defines database table structure

Schema → defines what data API accepts and returns
Example:
When user registers → they send:
json{
  "username": "John",
  "email": "john@gmail.com",
  "password": "123456"
}
Schema validates this data before it touches the database.
Also — when we return user data → we never return password. Schema controls that too.

Two types of schemas:
UserCreate  → data we ACCEPT (has password)
UserResponse → data we RETURN (no password)
