Before code — concept first.

What is JWT?
When you login → server gives you a token (like a hotel key card).
Every request after that → you show that token → server trusts you.
User logs in → server creates token → 
user sends token with every request → 
server verifies token → gives access

Why not just use username/password every time?
Sending password every request = dangerous. Token is safer and temporary.

Three parts of JWT:
header.payload.signature

eyJhbG...  →  who you are + expiry

Do you understand this concept?
Tell me in your own words what JWT does. 🧱You said: I think I've identified what I'm not understanding.I think I've identified what I'm not understanding.
