File: backend/app/utils/dependencies.py

This function does one job:
Extract token from request → 
verify it → 
find user in database → 
return user object
Here's the code. Read it first:
pythonfrom fastapi import Depends, HTTPException, status
from fastapi.security import OAuth2PasswordBearer
from sqlalchemy.orm import Session
from app.database.database import get_db
from app.models.user import User
from app.core.security import verify_token

oauth2_scheme = OAuth2PasswordBearer(tokenUrl="/auth/login")

def get_current_user(token: str = Depends(oauth2_scheme), db: Session = Depends(get_db)):
    payload = verify_token(token)
    if not payload:
        raise HTTPException(
            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,
            detail="Invalid token"
        )
    email = payload.get("sub")
    user = db.query(User).filter(User.email == email).first()
    if not user:
        raise HTTPException(
            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,
            detail="User not found"
        )
    return user

You tell me:
What does oauth2_scheme do in simple words? 🧱You said: take password and go to scheme to make it blanktake password and go to scheme to make it blankJun 10Claude responded: Not quite.Not quite. Simple answer:

oauth2_scheme automatically extracts the JWT token from the request header.

When frontend sends request it includes:
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbG...
oauth2_scheme grabs that token automatically. We don't do it manually.

