Before we code — concept:
When user submits login form:
1. React captures email + password
2. axios sends POST to /auth/login
3. Backend returns token
4. React stores token somewhere
5. Redirect to dashboard
Where should React store the token?
Options:

useState → lost on refresh
localStorage → stays even after refresh

Which one should we use and why? 🧱You said: local storagelocal storageJun 10Claude responded: Correct.Correct. 💪
Because:

Token must survive page refresh. If stored in useState → user gets logged out every refresh. localStorage persists.


