What is CORS?
Browser blocks React (port 5173) from talking to FastAPI (port 8000) because they're on different ports.
We need to tell FastAPI → "allow requests from React."

Open backend/app/main.py and add this:
pythonfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware

app.add_middleware(
    CORSMiddleware,
    allow_origins=["http://localhost:5173"],
    allow_credentials=True,
    allow_methods=["*"],
    allow_headers=["*"],
)
Add it after app = FastAPI().
Do it. Paste full main.py here. 🧱from app.database.database import Base, engine
from app.models.user import User
from app.models.workspace import  Workspace
from app.models.task import Task
from app.models.document import Document
from app.models.invite_code import InviteCode
from app.models.workspace_member import WorkspaceMember
from fastapi import FastAPI
from app.api.auth import router as auth_router
from app.api.workspace import router as workspace_router
app = FastAPI()
from fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware

app.add_middleware(
    CORSMiddleware,
    allow_origins=["http://localhost:5173"],
    allow_credentials=True,
    allow_methods=["*"],
    allow_headers=["*"],
)
app.include_router(auth_router, prefix="/auth", tags=["auth"])
app.include_router(workspace_router, prefix="/workspaces", tags=["workspaces"])
Base.metadata.create_all(bind=engine)

@app.get("/")
def home():
    return {"message": "CollabSpace Backend Running"}Show moreJun 10Claude responded: Almost.Almost. Move the CORS import to the top with other imports:
